      "source": [
        "from matplotlib import text\n",
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
        "import glob\n",
        "print(glob.glob(\"affiliate_orders_*.xlsx\"))\n",
        "\n",
        "# 1. Load and combine every export\n",
        "files = glob.glob(\"/content/**/affiliate_orders_*.xlsx\", recursive=True)\n",
        "print(len(files), files)\n",
        "\n",
        "df = pd.concat([pd.read_excel(f) for f in files], ignore_index=True)\n",
        "\n",
        "# remove duplicate orders (in case a file was uploaded twice)\n",
        "df = df.drop_duplicates(subset=[\"Order ID\", \"SKU ID\"])\n",
        "print(df.shape)   # should say 571 rows\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "# 2. Keep and rename the columns we need\n",
        "df = df[[\"Order date\", \"Product name\", \"Shop name\", \"Price\", \"Items sold\",\n",
        "         \"Items refunded\", \"Content ID\", \"Order type\", \"Order settlement status\",\n",
        "         \"GMV\", \"Est. standard commission\"]]\n",
        "df.columns = [\"date\", \"product\", \"shop\", \"price\", \"units\", \"refunded\",\n",
        "              \"video_id\", \"order_type\", \"status\", \"gmv\", \"commission\"]\n",
        "\n",
        "# 3. Clean\n",
        "df[\"date\"] = pd.to_datetime(df[\"date\"], dayfirst=True)\n",
        "df[\"video_id\"] = df[\"video_id\"].astype(str)\n",
        "df[\"month\"] = df[\"date\"].dt.to_period(\"M\").astype(str)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(df.shape, df[\"date\"].min(), df[\"date\"].max())\n",
        "\n",
        "# Chart 1: commission by brand\n",
        "df.groupby(\"shop\")[\"commission\"].sum().sort_values(ascending=False).head(5) \\\n",
        "  .plot(kind=\"bar\", color=\"#d6336c\", figsize=(7, 4), title=\"Commission by Brand\")\n",
        "plt.tight_layout(); plt.show()\n",
        "\n",
        "\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Wennalife is my top earner by a wide margin, so my income depends on one brand. I recommend testing a second beauty category to reduce that risk."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "SKpn_3NDGyu0"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "# Chart 2: top 10 videos\n",
        "df.groupby(\"video_id\")[\"commission\"].sum().sort_values(ascending=False).head(10) \\\n",
        "  .plot(kind=\"barh\", color=\"#d6336c\", figsize=(7, 4), title=\"Top 10 Videos by Commission\")\n",
        "plt.gca().invert_yaxis(); plt.tight_layout(); plt.show()\n",
        "\n",
        "\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/",
          "height": 407
        },
        "id": "bDzC-_YqIF5S",
        "outputId": "02b45785-6e0a-4b74-fc34-7f2eda13a562"
      },
      "execution_count": 2,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "display_data",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": [
              "<Figure size 700x400 with 1 Axes>"
            ],
            "image/png": "\n"
          },
          "metadata": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "You see which video is my top performer. It currenly holds 1.2M views and it my top paid commission. I would look at the conent itself (the way it was filmed, verbage, lighting, editing) to see what drew people to that video more than other videos."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "roItel-cJ-Zv"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "# Chart 3: monthly orders and commission\n",
        "monthly = df.groupby(\"month\").agg(orders=(\"video_id\", \"count\"),\n",
        "                                  commission=(\"commission\", \"sum\"))\n",
        "monthly.plot(subplots=True, figsize=(7, 5), marker=\"o\",\n",
        "             title=[\"Orders per Month\", \"Commission per Month\"])\n",
        "plt.tight_layout(); plt.show()\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/",
          "height": 507
        },
        "id": "kkvPtH8UIH44",
        "outputId": "32fcd761-04f8-47d5-ab8c-62ab2bda2567"
      },
      "execution_count": 3,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "display_data",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": [
              "<Figure size 700x500 with 2 Axes>"
            ],
            "image/png": "\n"
          },
          "metadata": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "As you can see there has been a decline in sales since January so I would take a look at the reasoning. I do see more people spending money on tiktok shop during the holidays, and after where they have more extra money to spend with the holidays being over. This is something to be evaluated to see how to get those sales continously."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "hgvRnrysIsRJ"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "print(df.groupby(\"order_type\").agg(orders=(\"video_id\", \"count\"),\n",
        "                                   gmv=(\"gmv\", \"sum\"),\n",
        "                                   commission=(\"commission\", \"sum\")))\n",
        "print(df[\"status\"].value_counts())\n",
        "print(df.groupby(\"status\")[\"gmv\"].sum())\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "FstQOYuDIpQG",
